{
  "slug": "roasted-carrot-and-potato-salad-with-herbs",
  "title": "Roasted carrot and potato salad with herbs",
  "blurb": "A warm salad of roasted root vegetables and courgette, tossed with fresh parsley and a light dressing.",
  "steps": [
    "Heat your oven to 200°C. Peel the carrots and cut them into batons about 1cm thick, then halve the potatoes if they are larger than a walnut.",
    "Cut the courgette into rounds about 1cm thick and peel and quarter the shallot. Toss all the vegetables in a roasting tin with half the olive oil, the cumin, oregano, salt and pepper.",
    "Roast for 20 minutes until the potatoes are tender and the edges of the vegetables are starting to brown.",
    "Roughly chop the parsley. Mix the remaining olive oil with the lemon juice in a large bowl.",
    "Add the hot roasted vegetables to the bowl and toss everything together with the parsley. Taste and adjust the seasoning if needed before serving warm."
  ],
